{"segments": [
 {"id": "c03-title-01", "scene": "c03-title", "lang": "en", "text": "Chapter three. Choose by the noun before it.", "pause": 0.5, "cues": ["title"]},
 {"id": "c03-title-02", "scene": "c03-title", "lang": "en", "text": "A relative works like an adjective. It follows a noun with al.", "pause": 0.3, "cues": ["sub"]},
 {"id": "c03-title-03", "scene": "c03-title", "lang": "en", "text": "And it matches that noun. Male or female. One or a group.", "pause": 0.7, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c03-ex-01", "scene": "c03-ex", "lang": "en", "text": "The boy who is in the house.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["ex:1"]},
 {"id": "c03-ex-02", "scene": "c03-ex", "lang": "ar", "text": "الْوَلَدُ الَّذِي فِي الْبَيْتِ", "pause": 0.6, "cues": ["ar:0"]},
 {"id": "c03-ex-03", "scene": "c03-ex", "lang": "en", "text": "The boy is one male. So we choose this one.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["note:1"]},
 {"id": "c03-ex-04", "scene": "c03-ex", "lang": "ar", "text": "الَّذِي", "pause": 0.6, "cues": ["ar:1"]},
 {"id": "c03-ex-05", "scene": "c03-ex", "lang": "en", "text": "The watch which is on the bed.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["ex:2"]},
 {"id": "c03-ex-06", "scene": "c03-ex", "lang": "ar", "text": "السَّاعَةُ الَّتِي عَلَى السَّرِيرِ", "pause": 0.6, "cues": ["ar:2"]},
 {"id": "c03-ex-07", "scene": "c03-ex", "lang": "en", "text": "The word for watch is feminine.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["note:2"]},
 {"id": "c03-ex-08", "scene": "c03-ex", "lang": "ar", "text": "السَّاعَةُ", "pause": 0.5, "cues": ["ar:3"]},
 {"id": "c03-ex-09", "scene": "c03-ex", "lang": "en", "text": "It is a thing, but a feminine one. So we choose this one.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c03-ex-10", "scene": "c03-ex", "lang": "ar", "text": "الَّتِي", "pause": 0.6, "cues": ["ar:4"]},
 {"id": "c03-ex-11", "scene": "c03-ex", "lang": "en", "text": "The boys who went out.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["ex:3"]},
 {"id": "c03-ex-12", "scene": "c03-ex", "lang": "ar", "text": "الْأَوْلَادُ الَّذِينَ خَرَجُوا", "pause": 0.6, "cues": ["ar:5"]},
 {"id": "c03-ex-13", "scene": "c03-ex", "lang": "en", "text": "A group of males. So we choose this one.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["note:3"]},
 {"id": "c03-ex-14", "scene": "c03-ex", "lang": "ar", "text": "الَّذِينَ", "pause": 0.6, "cues": ["ar:6"]},
 {"id": "c03-ex-15", "scene": "c03-ex", "lang": "en", "text": "The women who went out.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["ex:4"]},
 {"id": "c03-ex-16", "scene": "c03-ex", "lang": "ar", "text": "النِّسَاءُ اللَّاتِي خَرَجْنَ", "pause": 0.6, "cues": ["ar:7"]},
 {"id": "c03-ex-17", "scene": "c03-ex", "lang": "en", "text": "A group of females. So we choose this one.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["note:4"]},
 {"id": "c03-ex-18", "scene": "c03-ex", "lang": "ar", "text": "اللَّاتِي", "pause": 0.8, "cues": ["ar:8"]},
 {"id": "c03-tips-01", "scene": "c03-tips", "lang": "en", "text": "Two tips. First, look at the verb in the ṣila too. It matches the relative.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["show:1", "hl:It matches the relative"]},
 {"id": "c03-tips-02", "scene": "c03-tips", "lang": "en", "text": "For one male, the verb means he went out.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c03-tips-03", "scene": "c03-tips", "lang": "ar", "text": "الَّذِي خَرَجَ", "pause": 0.5, "cues": ["ar:0"]},
 {"id": "c03-tips-04", "scene": "c03-tips", "lang": "en", "text": "For one female, she went out.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c03-tips-05", "scene": "c03-tips", "lang": "ar", "text": "الَّتِي خَرَجَتْ", "pause": 0.5, "cues": ["ar:1"]},
 {"id": "c03-tips-06", "scene": "c03-tips", "lang": "en", "text": "For a group of males, they went out.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c03-tips-07", "scene": "c03-tips", "lang": "ar", "text": "الَّذِينَ خَرَجُوا", "pause": 0.5, "cues": ["ar:2"]},
 {"id": "c03-tips-08", "scene": "c03-tips", "lang": "en", "text": "For a group of females, the verb has its own ending.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c03-tips-09", "scene": "c03-tips", "lang": "ar", "text": "اللَّاتِي خَرَجْنَ", "pause": 0.7, "cues": ["ar:3"]},
 {"id": "c03-tips-10", "scene": "c03-tips", "lang": "en", "text": "Second. After a noun without al, Arabic leaves the relative out.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["show:2", "hl:leaves the relative out"]},
 {"id": "c03-tips-11", "scene": "c03-tips", "lang": "en", "text": "A student who passed came.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c03-tips-12", "scene": "c03-tips", "lang": "ar", "text": "جَاءَ طَالِبٌ نَجَحَ", "pause": 0.6, "cues": ["ar:5"]},
 {"id": "c03-tips-13", "scene": "c03-tips", "lang": "en", "text": "Here student has no al. So no relative comes after it.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c03-tips-14", "scene": "c03-tips", "lang": "en", "text": "In English we still say who. In Arabic, the clause comes straight after the noun.", "pause": 0.8, "cues": []}
]}
